# Using Storefront + Integration Agents Together
## Technical Collaboration Model for HCL Commerce Integration

---

## 1️⃣ YES - You CAN Use Both Agents Together

The two agents are **complementary, not competing**. They work on different layers of the same application:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   EDS Storefront (Frontend)                 │
│           🎨 STOREFRONT AGENT WORKS HERE                    │
│  - Product Detail Page (PDP) with Add to Cart button        │
│  - Shopping Cart display                                    │
│  - Mini-cart in header                                      │
│  - Cart page UI                                             │
│  - User interactions & event handling                       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓ (API calls via network)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           Adobe I/O Runtime (Middleware)                    │
│         🔧 INTEGRATION AGENT WORKS HERE                     │
│  - HCL Commerce API gateway                                 │
│  - Guest session management (WCToken, WCTrustedToken)       │
│  - Cart sync logic                                          │
│  - Authentication handling                                  │
│  - Data transformation                                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓ (API calls via network)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              HCL Commerce Backend (Commerce Engine)         │
│  - Product data & inventory                                 │
│  - Cart management                                          │
│  - Order processing                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 2️⃣ How the Agents Work Together

### **Phase 1: Integration Agent (Backend/Middleware) - Goes First**

The **Integration Starter Kit Agent** builds:

✅ **HCL Login Action**
- Runtime action that calls HCL login API
- Returns WCToken, WCTrustedToken, buyerId
- Handles guest session creation

✅ **Add to Cart Action**
- Runtime action that accepts product ID + quantity
- Calls HCL "Add to Cart" API with proper tokens
- Returns cart response with orderId, orderItemId
- Handles validation errors (out of stock, product not found, etc.)

✅ **Get Cart Action**
- Runtime action that retrieves current cart state
- Returns full cart data (items, prices, totals)
- Used to sync frontend display with backend

✅ **API Endpoints** (deployed to Adobe I/O Runtime)
```
POST /api/hcl/login           → Creates guest session
POST /api/hcl/cart/add        → Adds product to HCL cart
GET  /api/hcl/cart            → Gets current cart state
```

---

### **Phase 2: Storefront Agent (Frontend) - Comes After**

Once the Integration agent provides those API endpoints, I (Storefront Agent) can build:

✅ **Storefront Components**
- Modified "Add to Cart" button handler
  - Calls Integration API `/api/hcl/cart/add`
  - Shows success/error feedback
  - Updates local cart state

✅ **Mini-cart in Header**
  - Calls Integration API `/api/hcl/cart` to get cart data
  - Renders items, counts, totals
  - Real-time updates

✅ **Cart Page**
  - Fetches cart from Integration API
  - Displays all items with prices
  - Update quantity/remove item handlers

✅ **Status/Loading States**
  - Shows feedback while calling HCL APIs
  - Error handling & user messaging
  - Cart sync on page load

---

## 3️⃣ API Contract Between Agents

### **Critical Information You Must Get from Integration Agent:**

Before I can build the storefront, the Integration agent needs to provide:

#### **Endpoint 1: Add to Cart**
```
POST /api/hcl/cart/add
Content-Type: application/json

Request Body:
{
  "productId": "3074457345619160265",  // or "partNumber": "CLA022_220601"
  "quantity": 1,
  "productName": "Product Name"  // Optional, for display
}

Response (Success - 200):
{
  "success": true,
  "orderId": "764417",
  "orderItemId": "6545024",
  "cartTotal": "85.00",
  "itemCount": 2,
  "message": "Product added successfully"
}

Response (Error - 400/404/500):
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Product out of stock" | "Product not found" | "Server error",
  "message": "User-friendly error message"
}
```

#### **Endpoint 2: Get Cart**
```
GET /api/hcl/cart
Content-Type: application/json

Request Body:
(empty or can include filters)

Response (Success - 200):
{
  "success": true,
  "orderId": "764417",
  "items": [
    {
      "orderItemId": "6545024",
      "productId": "3074457345619160265",
      "partNumber": "BCL015_150101",
      "productName": "Product Name",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": "45.00",
      "orderItemPrice": "45.00",
      "orderItemInventoryStatus": "Available",
      "shippingCharge": "0.00",
      "salesTax": "0.00"
    },
    {
      "orderItemId": "6550001",
      "productId": "3074457345619160060",
      "partNumber": "BCL014_141301",
      "productName": "Another Product",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": "40.00",
      "orderItemPrice": "40.00",
      "orderItemInventoryStatus": "Available",
      "shippingCharge": "0.00",
      "salesTax": "0.00"
    }
  ],
  "cartTotals": {
    "itemCount": 2,
    "subtotal": "85.00",
    "shippingCharge": "0.00",
    "salesTax": "0.00",
    "grandTotal": "85.00",
    "currency": "USD"
  }
}

Response (Error - 401/500):
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Unauthorized" | "Server error",
  "message": "User-friendly error message"
}
```

#### **Endpoint 3: Remove from Cart** (Optional but recommended)
```
POST /api/hcl/cart/remove
Content-Type: application/json

Request Body:
{
  "orderItemId": "6545024"
}

Response (Success):
{
  "success": true,
  "orderId": "764417",
  "message": "Item removed successfully",
  "cartTotals": { ... }
}

Response (Error):
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Item not found",
  "message": "Unable to remove item"
}
```

---

## 4️⃣ What Integration Agent Should Build (Detailed Checklist)

Share this with your Integration Starter Kit agent:

### **Phase 1: Authentication & Session**
- [ ] Create Adobe I/O Runtime action for HCL guest login
- [ ] Store WCToken, WCTrustedToken in session/cache
- [ ] Handle token refresh/expiration
- [ ] Return session info to frontend

### **Phase 2: Cart Operations**
- [ ] Create action to add product to HCL cart (by productId)
- [ ] Create action to add product to HCL cart (by partNumber)
- [ ] Create action to get cart state from HCL
- [ ] Create action to remove item from HCL cart
- [ ] Create action to update item quantity in HCL cart
- [ ] Implement inventory validation (x_inventoryValidation flag)
- [ ] Handle error responses (out of stock, product not found, etc.)

### **Phase 3: API Gateway**
- [ ] Deploy as REST API endpoints in Adobe I/O Runtime
- [ ] Set up proper CORS headers for EDS frontend
- [ ] Implement request validation
- [ ] Implement error handling & logging
- [ ] Add authentication/security (if needed)

### **Phase 4: Data Transformation**
- [ ] Map HCL response format to storefront format
- [ ] Extract key fields (prices, inventory, product names)
- [ ] Format errors for frontend consumption
- [ ] Add success/failure flags

### **Phase 5: Testing & Documentation**
- [ ] Test all endpoints in Postman
- [ ] Document endpoint signatures
- [ ] Provide example requests/responses
- [ ] Share deployed endpoint URLs with storefront agent

---

## 5️⃣ What Storefront Agent Will Build (Your Changes)

Once Integration agent provides the API endpoints, I will handle:

### **A) Product Detail Page Changes**
