## 6️⃣ Execution Order

```
STEP 1: Integration Agent builds
├─ HCL authentication action
├─ Add to cart action
├─ Get cart action
├─ Remove from cart action
├─ Deploy to Adobe I/O Runtime
└─ Provide endpoint URLs & response formats

    ↓ (Pass info to Storefront Agent)

STEP 2: Storefront Agent builds
├─ Product Detail Page modifications
├─ Mini-cart component
├─ Cart page
├─ Event handlers
├─ Loading/error states
└─ Testing & validation

    ↓

STEP 3: End-to-End Testing
├─ Test add to cart flow
├─ Test mini-cart updates
├─ Test cart page display
├─ Test error scenarios
└─ Deploy to production
```

---

## 7️⃣ What You Need to Do NOW

### **For Integration Agent:**

1. **Ask them to build:**
   - HCL Cart Add API action (returns success/error)
   - HCL Cart Get API action (returns cart data)
   - HCL Cart Remove API action (optional)
   - Proper error handling
   - CORS-enabled endpoints

2. **Get from them:**
   - Deployed endpoint URLs
   - Response format (JSON structure)
   - Error response format
   - Any required headers/auth
   - Rate limiting info (if any)

3. **Example request to Integration Agent:**
   > "Please build the following Adobe I/O Runtime actions and provide endpoints:
   > - POST /api/hcl/cart/add - accepts {productId, quantity}
   > - GET /api/hcl/cart - returns current cart state
   > - POST /api/hcl/cart/remove - accepts {orderItemId}
   > - All responses should follow the format in [attach response formats above]"

### **For Me (Storefront Agent):**

Once you provide me with:
1. ✅ Deployed endpoint URLs from Integration Agent
2. ✅ Request/response JSON formats
3. ✅ Error handling expectations
4. ✅ Any auth headers needed

**Then I will build:**
- Modified Product Detail Page with Add to Cart integration
- Mini-cart updates in header
- Full Cart page display
- Error handling & user feedback
- Loading states
- Complete testing

